Open defects, staged: the trials here state the correct behaviour for two runtime gaps found in the project BEES triage (2026-10-23) that are not being fixed now: a monitor's DOWN message is never delivered (spec §15.4.8.6), and an FFI adapter whose guarded foreign call is in tail position faults (FFI spec §3.3). They fail today, and they have no .ascomp yet, so the host and board tree runs skip this directory. Run it by hand with make -C bees_gaps_open_addition integrate TRIAL_TARGET=host SILICA_COMPILER=... (or TRIAL_SUITES=bees_gaps_open_addition from trials/); see README.md. Each trial moves to a gated suite, with .ascomp goldens, once its fix is built and it passes on every host. The compile-rejection gaps from the same triage are in the compile_defects_*_addition siblings listed in README.md.
